    "body": "When the user edits text, check to see if the tabstop nodes have been emptied and pushed to the start of the line, as a heuristic to try to catch cases when the line the node was on was deleted at least up to the end of the node itself.\r\n\r\nThis heuristic has clear false-positives where it acts, so I did not see fit to fix the tests before getting confirmation that this is a direction that the plugin is willing to go.\r\n\r\nResolve #2400\r\n\r\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-05-01T14:25:45Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "This branch has changes that I made while experimenting with a way to fix #2400. I realize it diverges from the philosophy of the plugin, I created a PR from it just in case someone finds it interesting, *I don't expect for it to be merged*.\r\n\r\nThis is my first time writing a non-trivial amount of lua, and my first time writing a contribution to a neovim plugin. If you have the time to provide feedback on how/whether you would solve this, I'd appreciate it :smile:",
