            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the PR!\r\n\r\nAs described [here](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/2400#issuecomment-4359719773) this is a known and documented behavior. Primarily for reasons that there is no robust fix, as any text edit might be intentional from the user. The heuristic approach *might* work, but only if it is concise enough. +78 lines is, unfortunately, not it.\r\n\r\n> This is my first time writing a non-trivial amount of lua, and my first time writing a contribution to a neovim plugin. If you have the time to provide feedback on how/whether you would solve this, I'd appreciate it 😄\r\n\r\nThe Lua side of things looks okay. I didn't read too much into the code logic, but nothing bad catches the eye.\r\n\r\nThe way I've solved this is by workflow design and not code: always make sure to stop the snippet session if it is not needed. Also by making sure that the bad path does not cause errors and can be quickly fixed (like by pressing `<C-c>`).",
